---
description: Structure and conventions for the ApiResponse wrapper class used as the standard API response format across all RestControllers.
globs: **/src/main/java/**/ApiResponse.java
---
- Must use Lombok @Data, @NoArgsConstructor, and @AllArgsConstructor annotations.
- Must be a generic class ApiResponse<T>.
- Fields: `result` (String, "SUCCESS" or "ERROR"), `message` (String), `data` (T, nullable).
- Should provide static factory methods for convenience (e.g., `success(T data)`, `error(String message)`).
- Reference structure:

```java
@Data
@NoArgsConstructor
@AllArgsConstructor
public class ApiResponse<T> {
    private String result;    // "SUCCESS" or "ERROR"
    private String message;   // success or error message
    private T data;           // return object from service class, if successful

    public static <T> ApiResponse<T> success(String message, T data) {
        return new ApiResponse<>("SUCCESS", message, data);
    }

    public static ApiResponse<?> error(String message) {
        return new ApiResponse<>("ERROR", message, null);
    }
}
```
